Dear Team,

I would like to respectfully place on record certain facts and supporting information that were explained and demonstrated during the proceedings.

The non-compliance was never intentional, nor was there any intention on my part to disregard company policy. Throughout the period under discussion, I faced persistent seat booking challenges through the OfficePass system. Repeated booking attempts at my designated location frequently resulted in "No free seats available in this building" messages.

Further, when the office location in my area was subsequently moved to the ELCOT SEZ facility, I also attempted to book seats at the new location and continued to face the same seat availability issue. Screenshots supporting these booking attempts are attached for reference.

During the proceedings, I had explained the circumstances surrounding the office attendance challenges that I experienced and shared supporting information relating to the same. I had also explained that the seat booking challenges were communicated during the relevant period through Microsoft Teams with my Manager and that I was making efforts to address the issue while continuing to fulfil my project commitments. For completeness and ease of reference, I am attaching the relevant communications and supporting documents again along with this response.
While the circumstances evolved over a period of time, in hindsight, a more formal escalation may have helped provide greater visibility to the challenges being encountered.

I would also like to clarify that I did not remain disengaged from work during this period. I continued to actively support project delivery and operational commitments. This included participation in late-night deployment calls and support activities, often extending beyond normal working hours, including calls that continued until late night and early morning hours whenever required by project needs. At no point during this period was there any concern raised regarding my project delivery, availability, or commitment towards assigned responsibilities.
My Delivery Manager and project leadership are aware of my continued involvement and contributions throughout this period.

Additionally, I had explained during the proceedings that I had physically visited the office on my initial days; however, due to seating constraints, I was required to move between locations and was unable to secure a stable workspace. These experiences further contributed to the challenges I encountered regarding office attendance.

I would also like to submit that, during the period in question, I did not receive any specific non-compliance notification, attendance-related alert, or formal communication highlighting an ongoing attendance concern requiring immediate action from my side. While I appreciate that employees are expected to remain compliant with company policies, the absence of any such notification or escalation contributed to my understanding that the matter was primarily related to the operational challenges I was experiencing and was being addressed accordingly.

I respectfully submit that the circumstances were not a case of willful disobedience, intentional non-compliance, or refusal to follow company policy. Rather, the situation arose from a combination of persistent seat availability challenges, communication-related challenges, and the absence of a more formal escalation as the situation continued over a period of time.

I would also like to place on record that the issue has now been resolved after obtaining the required IP whitelisting, following which I have successfully booked seats and resumed office attendance. I have already started attending the office and remain fully committed to complying with all attendance requirements going forward.

In view of the above, I respectfully request that the explanations and supporting evidence presented during the proceedings, as well as the attached documentation, be considered as part of the record while reviewing this matter.

As the underlying issue has now been addressed and I have resumed office attendance, I respectfully request an opportunity to continue demonstrating my commitment to both my professional responsibilities and the company's attendance requirements going forward.


Thank you for your time and consideration.

Regards,
Kumaresh
